WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.940
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:10.020
YUFENG GUO: Hi.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.440
I'm Yufeng Guo, and I'm
here with Ameet Jani,

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.740
a Google expert in identity
and access management.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.336
Thanks for joining
me today, Ameet.

00:00:18.336 --> 00:00:19.710
AMEET JANI: Thanks
for having me.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:21.001
YUFENG GUO: Let's dig right in.

00:00:21.001 --> 00:00:23.940
So with the increase in
cyber attacks recently,

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.250
it's more important
than ever for IT

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.940
to stay in control of who
accesses company resources

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.980
while still enabling
employees to have

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:35.549
simpler and more intuitive
access to work apps and data.

00:00:35.549 --> 00:00:36.590
AMEET JANI: That's right.

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:38.520
Employees often work
outside the office,

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:41.130
as we know, in coffee
shops, hotels, airports,

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:43.860
and from home, so it's important
for companies to make sure

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:46.950
that employees access
apps and data securely.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:50.340
YUFENG GUO: So let's just
say I'm a chief information

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:53.110
security officer, and I
have a lot of employees

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:55.710
who want to access their
apps from outside the office,

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:58.399
like you mentioned, and
from their personal devices.

00:00:58.399 --> 00:00:59.940
AMEET JANI: OK, so
you want employees

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.647
being productive
from anywhere, but IT

00:01:01.647 --> 00:01:03.480
wants to make sure that
they are controlling

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:04.730
what data they have access to.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:08.331
So let's take this example.

00:01:08.331 --> 00:01:10.330
You have a sales rep using
their personal device

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:11.860
and is about to close a deal.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:14.720
You want it done securely,
safely, and successfully.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:17.630
We can see that our sales rep is
using a corporate laptop that's

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:20.320
approved by IT, but they're
also using a personal tablet

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.650
device that hasn't
been approved by IT.

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:25.150
The sales rep wants to be able
to use their tablet to access

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:28.744
CRM systems and G Suite, and
corporate IT has to allow that.

00:01:28.744 --> 00:01:30.160
YUFENG GUO: Right,
so the employee

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:34.307
wants to use their personal
tablet and access work data.

00:01:34.307 --> 00:01:35.140
AMEET JANI: Exactly.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:36.880
But the problem is
that personal tablets

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:38.530
don't have as many
security controls

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:39.739
as the corporate device does.

00:01:39.739 --> 00:01:41.613
YUFENG GUO: And so can
you talk a little more

00:01:41.613 --> 00:01:42.810
about the risk of that?

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:44.680
AMEET JANI: Well, the risk is
that if an attacker exploits

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:46.346
the weaknesses on
this personal tablet--

00:01:46.346 --> 00:01:48.560
let's say that they
use OS version flaws

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:49.780
and things like that--

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:51.280
they can get access
to apps and data

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:52.571
that they shouldn't be able to.

00:01:52.571 --> 00:01:53.380
YUFENG GUO: Got it.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:58.240
So as a CSO, how can I make
employees more productive

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:00.292
using these personal devices?

00:02:00.292 --> 00:02:02.500
AMEET JANI: Well as a first
step, what you want to do

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:04.210
is only give our
sales rep access

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:06.220
to apps on their personal
device if they're

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:07.630
in the right context.

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:09.729
Using Google Cloud's
Access Context Manager,

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:12.190
you can define a policy
for these personal devices

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:14.650
to only allow them to access
some apps while the employee's

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:15.877
in the office.

00:02:15.877 --> 00:02:17.710
So if you go to our
sales rep in the office,

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:20.800
they can now access their CRM
system and G Suite applications

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:23.650
from their personal device and
from their corporate laptop.

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:25.397
YUFENG GUO: So that
lets my sales reps

00:02:25.397 --> 00:02:26.980
be productive on
their personal tablet

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.569
while they're in the office
and can be on a secure network.

00:02:29.569 --> 00:02:30.610
AMEET JANI: That's right.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:34.090
YUFENG GUO: And so this is
great for my employees that

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:35.770
are working in the
office all the time.

00:02:35.770 --> 00:02:37.900
But then what about when
they leave the office?

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:39.022
AMEET JANI: Good question.

00:02:39.022 --> 00:02:40.480
It's common today
for our employees

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:42.580
to be working
outside the office.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:45.040
Let's say our sales rep
goes to the coffee shop,

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.260
and they log in
using public Wi-Fi.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:50.210
This is a problem because they
may not be a secure network.

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:52.900
YUFENG GUO: Right, public
Wi-Fi is often not so secure.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.650
AMEET JANI: Public
Wi-Fi might be secure,

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:55.780
but we need to be careful.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:58.030
Otherwise, attackers can
exploit vulnerabilities

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:00.962
in these networks to get
access to users' devices

00:03:00.962 --> 00:03:02.920
or they could easily look
over users' shoulders

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:05.530
to see sensitive data
or password information.

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:06.310
YUFENG GUO: Yeah.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:09.460
So the way I've always done this
is just by logging into a VPN

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:11.620
when I'm accessing
one of these networks.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:13.550
AMEET JANI: Well, VPNs
might do the trick.

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:15.160
But they can be
one-size-fits-all,

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:17.730
and they can be a pain
for employees to log into.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.440
We have another way of
giving context-aware access

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:22.750
to applications
using Google Cloud.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:25.900
Using Google Cloud Services like
Identity-Aware Proxy in Cloud

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:28.420
Identity, we can gather
information from the employees

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:31.210
context, like the device
they're logging in from,

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.230
the type of network
they're connected to,

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.380
and we can set up a
rule that blocks access

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:37.900
to sensitive applications
on personal devices

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:41.290
when they're in a situation
like this using public Wi-Fi.

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:44.200
So if our sales rep moves from
the office to the coffee shop,

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.475
this triggers a context
change in Identity-Aware Proxy

00:03:46.475 --> 00:03:47.920
in Cloud Identity.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:50.920
And when our sales rep tries
to access their CRM or G Suite

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:53.470
app, they can access the app
from the corporate device

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:55.480
because this is a
more secure device.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.220
But for their personal
device, the app

00:03:57.220 --> 00:04:00.040
is blocked because of this
heightened security need.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:01.790
Why don't you give it a try?

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:03.390
YUFENG GUO: All right.

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:04.860
So OK, so that's blocked.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:07.360
AMEET JANI: Here, you
can see it's failed.

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:09.080
And here, the access is granted.

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:09.880
YUFENG GUO: Got it.

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:13.660
So as employers move around
and their context changes,

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:15.910
that changes their
access to different apps.

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:16.839
AMEET JANI: Exactly.

00:04:16.839 --> 00:04:18.459
So now, the sales
rep can still be

00:04:18.459 --> 00:04:20.800
productive outside the
office, but their access

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:23.960
to certain apps on certain
devices are restricted.

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:27.040
And as a CSO, you can
see granular controls

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.200
to add heightened
security in some context.

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:34.052
Let's say your sales rep
is closing a deal overseas

00:04:34.052 --> 00:04:36.010
and needs to travel to
an international country

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:37.426
that your security
team has deemed

00:04:37.426 --> 00:04:38.755
to be a restricted country.

00:04:38.755 --> 00:04:40.750
If the sales rep
accesses their app

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:42.940
from a network like
the hotel Wi-Fi,

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:45.060
attackers may exploit
vulnerabilities

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:48.606
in the network to access the
sales rep's app and data.

00:04:48.606 --> 00:04:50.230
YUFENG GUO: All right,
so I should just

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:53.470
lock down all access to apps
when employees are traveling

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:54.284
to these countries.

00:04:54.284 --> 00:04:55.450
AMEET JANI: Not necessarily.

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:57.280
It's often the case
that executives

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:59.860
need to be able to work from
these higher security threat

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:02.950
countries, and they need to
access some sensitive data

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:04.450
to get work done.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:07.540
Using Google Cloud, you can add
an additional level of security

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:10.140
for high-risk context like this.

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:12.040
In Access Context
Manager, I can set

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:15.190
a rule that blocks all
access to apps except G Suite

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:18.014
Gmail from these countries and
only from a corporate device.

00:05:18.014 --> 00:05:19.180
Why don't you give it a try?

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:22.070
On the personal device, why
don't you try accessing Gmail?

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:23.142
YUFENG GUO: Sure.

00:05:23.142 --> 00:05:25.320
I'm going to flip
over to Gmail here.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:29.490
And say try to type in
Gmail, and I hit Enter.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:30.824
And it looks like we're blocked.

00:05:30.824 --> 00:05:31.948
AMEET JANI: You're blocked.

00:05:31.948 --> 00:05:33.450
But from a corporate
device, you'll

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:35.920
lose access to the
confidential data.

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:37.950
YUFENG GUO: OK, so
no CRM access for me.

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:38.783
AMEET JANI: Exactly.

00:05:38.783 --> 00:05:41.040
But when you check your
email, it'll continue to work.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.320
YUFENG GUO: Great.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:43.320
AMEET JANI: So now
when the sales rep

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.720
tries to access this application
from the corporate device,

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:46.890
everything works as planned.

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:49.560
And the only app they can access
is, of course, the G Suite app

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:51.870
because that's what's
been termed to be safe.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:54.600
YUFENG GUO: So that means the
sales rep doesn't have access

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:57.240
to all the apps with sensitive
data in this country,

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:58.770
but they can still
be productive.

00:05:58.770 --> 00:05:59.860
AMEET JANI: Exactly.

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:02.280
So now, even in these
high-risk context,

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:04.110
you can better keep
employees productive

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:05.840
and your apps and data safe.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:07.470
YUFENG GUO: This is great.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:11.580
I think it might finally be time
to get rid of that Legacy VPN.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:13.800
Ameet, thanks so much
for talking to us today

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.110
and teaching me how to
keep a mobile workforce

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:17.730
productive and secure.

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:19.600
AMEET JANI: My pleasure, Yufeng.

